  "ingredients": [
    "5 ounce cream cheese (softened)",
    "1/4 cup mozzarella cheese (grated)",
    "8 medium jalapeno pepper",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1/4 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/2 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (like mrs. dash)",
    "8 ounce bacon"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Wash the jalapeño peppers. Line a baking sheet with foil and remove the stems from the peppers.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5442.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice each pepper in half, cutting them as evenly as possible.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5452.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a spoon to scrape out the insides of the peppers (you can leave a few seeds for extra heat if you'd like).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5458.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, combine the cream cheese, mozzarella, and spices — I used salt, pepper, and Mrs. Dash, but feel free to mix these up!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5460.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fill half of the pepper halves with the cream cheese mixture, creating a mound that the other halves will fit on top of.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5469.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Close the peppers back up by pressing the empty halves on top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5475.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wrap each pepper in bacon, starting from the bottom and working your way up to the top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5477.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20–25 minutes or until the bacon is cooked through and beginning to crisp up. Broil for an additional 2–3 minutes to get a darker color and more crisp on the bacon.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/IMG_5482.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spicy-jalapeno-poppers/#wprm-recipe-51161-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
